Changes to Madeira itself (third_party/madeira). Applied by scripts/apply-patches.sh.

- build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c: 32-bit stacks grow again. The WOW_TEB stack limits are guest
  addresses, so a guard page fault (host address) is compared after adding the base of the
  thread's 4 GB window, on both the signal and the Mach exception path. [wow-stack-ovf] prints
  what filled a 32-bit stack when one overflows.
- build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c: a store by native code (outside the JIT pool) into an RWX
  page that FEX write-trapped for self-modifying code completes through the alias, as Windows
  lets a syscall write such a page. It used to wreck the thread (32-bit wrap_glGetError).
- build/ntdll-unix/thread_ios.c: [bad-stack] diagnostic line next to "Exception frame is not
  in stack limits"; no behaviour change.
- app/Madeira/WineProcessBridge.m: MADEIRA_VULKAN_DEFAULT, the Vulkan choice when madeira.cfg
  has none (the app sets moltenvk).
- app/Madeira/Winios/WiniosGL.m: the OpenGL presenter marks the game's window as presenting
  through Metal, so its empty GDI frame no longer covers the picture.

